{
  "_about": [
    "Public, citable wM-Bus / OMS test vectors for validating the decoder in",
    "wmbuslib.decrypt_frame. These are reference vectors with published keys, not",
    "default-key guesses: they prove the AES-CBC path, the Mode-5 IV construction",
    "and the record parser are correct, and never unlock a real meter.",
    "",
    "Sources: the OMS Spec Vol.2 Annex N Security Profile A example key, and the",
    "MIT-licensed wmbusmeters test suite - the per-driver test frames in",
    "drivers/src/*.xmq, the aggregate meter tables in tests/*.sh, and the telegram",
    "bodies in simulations/*. Each entry names where it came from.",
    "",
    "expect_prefix is the first bytes of the correct-key plaintext. For standard",
    "Mode 5 (CI 72/7A) that begins with the OMS idle-filler marker 2F2F; for the",
    "Qundis CI-78 wrapper it is the wrapper payload. run_vectors.py asserts the",
    "prefix AND that a bit-flipped wrong key does NOT reproduce it.",
    "",
    "known_gaps lists vectors whose security mode this decoder does not implement",
    "(Kamstrup compact CI 8D, kamwater CCM/GCM auth-tag). They are documented, not",
    "run, so the corpus stays honest about coverage."
  ],
